  "decision_conditions": [
    "A full assessment of the application as submitted could not\r\nbe carried out in&nbsp;relation to the principle of development pertaining to\r\nthe loss of the existing commercial retail unit (Use Class E(a)) as\r\ninsufficient information was provided to justify the loss. As such the\r\nprinciple of the development could not be fully determined and is therefore&nbsp;contrary\r\nto policy 42 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The application as submitted,&nbsp;comprises of inconsistent\r\nplans where the proposed ground floor plan\r\nillustrates the intention to remove the fenestration that faces onto Millicent\r\nRoad but the existing/proposed elevations have been illustrated without the\r\nremoval of said fenestration. Therefore a true assessment of the proposal could\r\nnot be made with regard to Policy 53 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan\r\nPart 1 (2024).",
    "The application as submitted,&nbsp;comprises of insufficient\r\ninformation with regard to the proposed business activities. Therefore, a true\r\nassessment of neighbour amenity impacts could not be assessed with regard to\r\nPolicy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024)."
  ],
